# Glow HD Engine — HDE-EPIC037 final repo-docs sweep

The Glow HD Engine is a deterministic Human Design engine and CLI that emits governed, canonically serialized bytes. PF-Canon remains authoritative (titles only: PF05 — CLI/API/Vendor Ref, PF12 — Schemas & Artifacts, PF14 — Mechanics Guide, PF19 — QA Guide, PF20 — Phased Epics).

## Overview

- Public Reader v1 and CLI share the canonical emitter and serializer; AB↔BA and two-run identity proofs cover public bytes.
- Error responses use the canonical schema-v1 envelope with typed error tokens and JSON discipline under closed rails.
- Evidence posture is governed: human Evidence Index under `docs/evidence/INDEX.json`, machine mirror under `artifacts/evidence_index.jsonl`, and `.path_proof.txt` siblings for governed artifacts.
- What HDE-EPIC030 clarifies:
  - HDE-EPIC030 is a Dissolution Pass 3 closure slice for still-fluid internal/admin and dev-only surfaces; it is not a public-surface redesign pass.
  - EPIC030 evidence families are governed under `audit/qa/hde-epic030/pr-01/` through `audit/qa/hde-epic030/pr-05/` with sibling `.path_proof.txt` files for each artifact.
  - PR-01 normalization evidence records zero-weight handoff, invalid viewer-preference fail-closed behavior, and canonical compare outputs (`zero_weight_handoff.json`, `invalid_viewer_prefs.log`, `normalization_canonical_compare.log`).
  - PR-02 dev sampler evidence preserves the existing `/internal/dev/sampler` POST-only dev harness posture (APP_ENV-gated) and records IDs-only plus seed metadata and two-run identity (`dev_sampler_http_headers.txt`, `dev_sampler_http_body.json`, `dev_sampler_seed_only.json`, `dev_sampler_two_run_identity.json`).
  - PR-03 compat bindings capture category-order binding, compat identity hash, and AB↔BA parity evidence (`category_order_binding.log`, `compat_identity_binding.log`, `compat_parity_binding.log`).
  - PR-04 band-threshold evidence binds thresholds to the existing constants-pack home (`artifacts/thresholds/band_edges.json`) and records tuning diffs/identity (`band_edges_binding.log`, `band_thresholds_diff.json`, `band_thresholds_identity_hash.txt`).
