  - Conjunction compute is shipped on the compat path: deterministic `conjunction` output is produced by the same canonical emitter path used for compat payloads (`engine.compat.compute.conjunction_public` / `conjunction_public_resolved` + `engine.presenter.emitter`). Contract tests cover canonical-byte stability and AB↔BA identity expectations.
  - CLI `showcompat` supports conjunction mode via `--conjunction` with either `--user-a/--user-b`, `--a-file/--b-file`, `--pair-file`, or stdin pair payload input. Stdout must end with exactly one LF; CRLF is rejected with explicit error codes (`STDOUT_MISSING_LF`, `STDOUT_CRLF`). In conjunction mode, unresolved user inputs run through SAFE-rails BodyGraph resolution (default closed) and may return explicit refusal codes such as `PROVIDER_REFUSED`.
  - Dev-only conjunction preview routes exist for sampler/reader/writer under `/dev/sampler/conjunction`, `/dev/reader/conjunction`, and `/dev/writer/conjunction` (catalog methods are currently GET). These are APP_ENV-gated and only available for `dev|test|local`.
