- EPIC031 SAFE rails evidence: `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-01/open_rails_policy_proof.json`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-01/retry_backoff_429_proof.json`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-01/closed_default_open_exception_rails.json`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-02/vendor_keys_only.sample.jsonl`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-02/keys_only_log_redaction.json`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-02/bounded_label_observability.json`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-02/secret_redaction_scan.log`, `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-03/evidence_family_map.json`, and `audit/qa/hde-epic031/pr-03/safe_rails_evidence_coherence.json` (all governed with `.path_proof.txt` siblings and Index/Mirror rows).
- Orientation and sanity checks: `python tools/evidence/update_evidence_index.py` (write) then `python tools/evidence/orientation_demo.py` (write) followed by their `--check` variants; `python tools/evidence/run_sanity_pipeline.py` (closed rails); `ci/checks/check_mirror_schema.sh` enforces mirror schema/self-record/path-proof discipline.
- Registry report: `python tools/generate_registry_report.py` → `artifacts/registry/registry_report.json`.
- Evidence index updater: `python tools/evidence/update_evidence_index.py` refreshes Index/Mirror bindings after regenerating governed artifacts.
- EPIC027 acceptance scaffolding: `docs/acceptance_map_epic027.json` and `audit/qa/hde-epic027/token_evidence_matrix.md` bind the canonical 17-token ledger to evidence/tests, with viability gate output in `audit/qa/hde-epic027/acceptance_map_viability.log` and same-run QA logs under `audit/qa/hde-epic027/checks/<check_id>/primary.log`. Governed close-pack artifacts live in `audit/EPIC-027_MANIFEST.json` and `audit/EPIC-027_close_report.md`.
- Known canon mismatch: PF20 D3 references a provenance note, but the implemented `/internal/version` posture uses the PF10-style governed two-run/coupling proof log as the single provenance record; see PF20 for canonical posture.

## Testing (minimal)

- Showcompat canonical bytes and LF discipline: `tests/cli/test_cli_canonical_bytes.py::test_showcompat_stdout_is_canonical`.
- Stream discipline (stdout-only success; stderr-only failures): `tests/cli/test_cli_usage_and_errors.py`.
- Compat endpoint contract + catalog tests: `tests/http/test_compat_endpoint_contract.py`, `tests/http/test_endpoint_catalog.py`.
- Reader A7 transport invariants: `tests/http/test_reader_a7_transport.py`.
- EPIC024 bootstrap classification: `tests/qa/test_epic024_bootstrap_status.py` (missing pytest → FAIL_TOOLING, nonzero test failures → FAIL_BEHAVIOR).
- Evidence index snapshot validation: `tests/evidence/test_evidence_index_snapshot.py` (RFC3339 UTC validation and mirror JSONL parsing behavior).
- Arrays-as-sets proof: `tests/compare/test_arrays_as_sets.py`.
- Evidence/index coverage: `python -m pytest tests/evidence tests/ops/test_evidence_index.py`.
- EPIC022 acceptance scaffolding: `tests/qa/test_epic022_acceptance_scaffold.py`.
- Error/Reader parity (closed rails refusal and env pins): `tests/cli/test_errors_parity.py::test_http_and_cli_parity`.
- EPIC031 local SAFE rails checks: `python tools/evidence/generate_epic031_pr01_provider_gate.py`, `python tools/evidence/generate_epic031_pr02_log_posture.py --check`, and `python tools/evidence/generate_epic031_pr03_evidence_coherence.py --check`; job descriptors also pin `python -m pytest tests/bodygraph/test_resolver_vendor.py -q` and `python -m pytest tests/bodygraph/test_vendor_client.py -q` without live vendor calls.
